             (:domain "sequence segments" :code "(define segments (list (list 'a 'b) (list 'c 'd)))\n(concatenate! segments)")
     )
     :explanation "In each case, the nested structure is flattened into a single-level list by relinking the cons cells. The original structure is destroyed in the process."
     :meta "The shape transfers because the operation is about combining sequences while reusing their underlying structure.")
    (:eng "Destructive operations modify their arguments, so the caller must be aware of this side effect."
     :math "The result of concatenate! should not be eq? to the original list but should be equal to the result of applying append."
